<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Terp Notes: class notes and study guides from UMD students' }) %>
</head>
<body class="tn-app tn-home">
    <%- include('partials/publicnav') %>

    <main id="main">
        <section class="tn-hero">
            <% if (loggedout) { %>
                <div class="tn-alert tn-alert-ok" role="status" style="max-width: 420px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;">You're logged out. See you next time.</div>
            <% } %>
            <span class="tn-eyebrow"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Free for every Terp</span>
            <h1>Notes from Terps who already took your class.</h1>
            <p>Lecture notes, study guides and exam prep for UMD courses, shared by students. Search by course, professor or term and download what you need.</p>
            <div class="tn-actions">
                <a href="/register" class="tn-btn tn-btn-primary tn-btn-lg">Sign up with your UMD email</a>
                <a href="/login" class="tn-btn tn-btn-outline tn-btn-lg">Log in</a>
            </div>
            <p class="tn-fine">Takes a minute. Only @umd.edu and @terpmail.umd.edu addresses can join.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="tn-preview" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="tn-preview-frame">
                <div class="tn-preview-bar">
                    <div class="tn-fake-search">
                        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"/></svg>
                        <b>CMSC132</b>&nbsp;recursion
                    </div>
                </div>
                <ul class="tn-files">
                    <li class="tn-file">
                        <span class="tn-file-type tn-type-pdf">PDF</span>
                        <div class="tn-file-main">
                            <span class="tn-file-name">Lecture 7: Recursion and the call stack.pdf</span>
                            <div class="tn-file-meta"><span class="tn-chip">CMSC132</span><span class="tn-cat">Lecture Notes</span><span>Spring 2026</span></div>
                            <div class="tn-file-sub"><span>2 days ago</span><span>840 KB</span><span>38 downloads</span></div>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tn-btn tn-btn-outline tn-btn-sm">Download</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="tn-file">
                        <span class="tn-file-type tn-type-docx">DOCX</span>
                        <div class="tn-file-main">
                            <span class="tn-file-name">Midterm 2 study guide, worked examples.docx</span>
                            <div class="tn-file-meta"><span class="tn-chip">CMSC132</span><span class="tn-cat">Study Guide</span><span>Fall 2025</span></div>
                            <div class="tn-file-sub"><span>Oct 29</span><span>120 KB</span><span>64 downloads</span></div>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tn-btn tn-btn-outline tn-btn-sm">Download</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="tn-file">
                        <span class="tn-file-type tn-type-pdf">PDF</span>
                        <div class="tn-file-main">
                            <span class="tn-file-name">Practice problems: recursive backtracking.pdf</span>
                            <div class="tn-file-meta"><span class="tn-chip">CMSC132</span><span class="tn-cat">Homework</span><span>Spring 2026</span></div>
                            <div class="tn-file-sub"><span>Nov 2</span><span>410 KB</span><span>21 downloads</span></div>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tn-btn tn-btn-outline tn-btn-sm">Download</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <section class="tn-section" aria-labelledby="features">
            <div class="tn-section-head">
                <p class="tn-kicker">Why Terp Notes</p>
                <h2 id="features">Find the right notes in seconds.</h2>
                <p>Everything is organized by UMD course code, so you skip the group-chat scroll and the dead Google Drive links.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tn-grid">
                <div class="tn-feature">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"/></svg>
                    <h3>Search that knows your schedule</h3>
                    <p>Filter by course, professor, term and type: lecture notes, study guides, exams and homework.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tn-feature">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 16V4M6 10l6-6 6 6M4 20h16"/></svg>
                    <h3>Upload in a few taps</h3>
                    <p>Drag in PDFs, slides, docs or photos from your phone. Add the course once for a whole batch.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tn-feature">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 4 6v6c0 4.5 3.4 8.3 8 9 4.6-.7 8-4.5 8-9V6l-8-3Z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
                    <h3>Every file is scanned</h3>
                    <p>Uploads are checked by 70+ antivirus engines before anyone can download them.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tn-feature">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m3 7 9 6 9-6"/></svg>
                    <h3>Terps only</h3>
                    <p>Every account is verified with a UMD email, and reported files are reviewed by moderators.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tn-feature">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h6v6H4zM14 4h6v6h-6zM4 14h6v6H4z"/><path d="M17 14v6M14 17h6"/></svg>
                    <h3>Bring notes from your apps</h3>
                    <p>Import from Google Drive, Notion or OneNote, and use your notes in ChatGPT or Claude.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tn-feature">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="2" width="10" height="20" rx="2"/><path d="M11 18h2"/></svg>
                    <h3>Works on your phone</h3>
                    <p>Check a study guide on the Shuttle-UM or download a whole course at once on your laptop.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <div class="tn-band">
            <section class="tn-section" aria-labelledby="how">
                <div class="tn-section-head">
                    <p class="tn-kicker">How it works</p>
                    <h2 id="how">Three steps, then you're studying.</h2>
                </div>
                <ol class="tn-steps">
                    <li><h3>Sign up</h3><p>Use your @umd.edu or @terpmail.umd.edu address and confirm the email we send.</p></li>
                    <li><h3>Find your course</h3><p>Search a course code like CMSC131 or a professor, then filter by term.</p></li>
                    <li><h3>Share back</h3><p>Upload your own notes when you can. That's what keeps it free for everyone.</p></li>
                </ol>
            </section>
        </div>

        <section class="tn-section" aria-labelledby="faq">
            <div class="tn-section-head">
                <p class="tn-kicker">Questions</p>
                <h2 id="faq">Good to know</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="tn-faq">
                <details>
                    <summary>Is it really free?</summary>
                    <p>Yes. No ads, no paywall and no credit card. Terp Notes is a student project run by Terps.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Is this run by the University of Maryland?</summary>
                    <p>No. Terp Notes is independent and not affiliated with or endorsed by UMD. We ask for a UMD email only to keep the community to Terps.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>What can I share?</summary>
                    <p>Your own notes, study guides and summaries. Don't upload anything your instructor has said not to share, and follow UMD's Code of Academic Integrity. The full rules are in our <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>What file types work?</summary>
                    <p>PDFs, Word, PowerPoint and Excel files, images, text and code files, and zip archives, up to 100 MB each.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>What do you do with my data?</summary>
                    <p>We store your name, UMD email and the files you upload. We never sell data. Details are in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
                </details>
            </div>
        </section>

        <div class="tn-band">
            <section class="tn-section tn-cta">
                <h2>Your next exam is easier with better notes.</h2>
                <p>Join with your UMD email and start searching in under a minute.</p>
                <div class="tn-actions">
                    <a href="/register" class="tn-btn tn-btn-primary tn-btn-lg">Create a free account</a>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/footer') %>

    <script>
        // A signed-in student who lands here from the back button goes straight to their notes.
        fetch('/api/session-status', { credentials: 'include' })
            .then(r => (r.ok ? r.json() : null))
            .then(d => { if (d && d.loggedIn) window.location.replace('/dashboard'); })
            .catch(() => {});
    </script>
</body>
</html>
